---
// Faq.astro - Technical & Compliance Accordion FAQ
---

<section id="faq" class="py-16 px-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <div class="text-center mb-12">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyber-cyan/10 border border-cyber-cyan/30 text-cyber-cyan text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase mb-3">
      <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-sm shrink-0">help</span>
      TECHNICAL &amp; ARCHITECTURE FAQ
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
      Architecture, Performance & Compliance
    </h2>
    <p class="text-cyber-muted text-base max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      Everything security architects, CTOs, and engineering teams need to know about <code class="font-mono text-cyber-neon text-sm">pii-veil</code>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ Accordion -->
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <!-- Item 1 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-neon/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-neon transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-sm">01.</span>
          How does the Reversible Roundtrip work without persisting data?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-neon transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          When you call <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs bg-slate-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">engine.redact()</code>, the engine performs a linear-time <code class="text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs">O(N)</code> multi-pattern scan powered by Aho-Corasick automata.
        </p>
        <p>
          Identified sensitive values (such as credit cards, emails, or government IDs) are isolated in an ephemeral, <strong class="text-cyber-cyan">in-memory volatile Vault</strong> inside your application process, replacing them with unique cryptographic placeholders (e.g. <code translate="no" class="notranslate text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">[CREDIT_CARD_1]</code>). The external LLM processes only the sanitized text. When receiving the response or token stream from the LLM, calling <code class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-xs">vault.restore()</code> deterministically re-injects the original plaintext values. Once the Vault object is dropped or goes out of scope, all sensitive data is immediately cleared from RAM.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 2 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-cyan/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-cyan transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-sm">02.</span>
          Does any data ever leave my infrastructure or browser (Zero-Egress)?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-cyan transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-white">Absolutely zero data ever leaves.</strong> <code class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-xs">pii-veil</code> has no backend servers, makes zero external network calls, includes no hidden telemetry, and requires no internet connection to operate.
        </p>
        <p>
          The engine runs 100% <em>in-process</em> as a native compiled Rust library, via C-ABI / PyO3 in Python, N-API in Node.js, static binaries via the CLI, or compiled directly to WebAssembly (WASM) inside the client's browser.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 3 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-neon/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-neon transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-sm">03.</span>
          Why is it up to 200x faster than Microsoft Presidio?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-neon transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          Traditional Python-based DLP solutions (such as Presidio) rely on heavy NLP models (spaCy / transformers) and sequential regular expressions with exponential backtracking (NFA), introducing <strong>15 to 50 ms of overhead per request</strong> and creating severe bottlenecks due to the Python Global Interpreter Lock (GIL).
        </p>
        <p>
          <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">pii-veil</code> compiles directly to bare-metal machine code. It leverages a single deterministic finite automaton (DFA) coupled with direct CPU register arithmetic checks (Luhn, Mod-11, Mod-23, Mod-97), processing typical LLM payloads in <strong>sub-100 microseconds</strong> while sustaining over <strong>250,000 req/sec per core</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 4 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-purple/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-purple transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-purple font-mono text-sm">04.</span>
          Which compliance frameworks and regulatory standards are covered?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-purple transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong class="text-white">GDPR / RGPD (European Union):</strong> Art. 32 effective pseudonymization of personal data before processing by third-party model providers.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">PCI-DSS v4.0:</strong> Requirement 3.4 regarding zero exposure of readable cardholder PANs in logs, analytics, or LLM prompt traces.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">HIPAA (United States):</strong> Safe Harbor de-identification method removing all 18 protected health information (PHI) identifiers.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">SOC 2 Type II:</strong> Confidentiality controls and accident-prevention mechanisms for infrastructure secrets and API keys (AWS, GitHub, JWT, OpenAI).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 5 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-amber-400/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-amber-400 transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-sm">05.</span>
          Can I define custom detectors or proprietary pattern rules?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-amber-400 transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          Yes. In addition to the 19 built-in detectors and 12 global national ID validators backed by mathematical checksums, you can register custom regular expressions, contextual keyword dictionaries, or pluggable <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">NerDetector</code> providers tailored to your industry (e.g., internal insurance policy numbers, proprietary patient record IDs, or employee identifiers).
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 6: Layered Defense & NER -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-cyan/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-cyan transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-sm">06.</span>
          Does pii-veil replace Named Entity Recognition (NER) for free-text names?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-cyan transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          No, and deliberately so. Forcing 100% of LLM prompts through heavy transformer models (like Presidio, spaCy, or RoBERTa) introduces <strong>30 to 50 ms of artificial latency</strong> and consumes gigabytes of memory per container, making token streaming sluggish and expensive.
        </p>
        <p>
          Instead, enterprise teams deploy the <strong class="text-cyber-cyan">Layered Defense (Fast Path / Selective Slow Path)</strong> pattern:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Tier 0 (pii-veil Fast Path):</strong> Intercepts 100% of traffic in <strong>sub-100 microseconds</strong>, mathematically scrubbing credit cards, IBANs, national IDs (DNI/SSN/CUIT), API keys, JWTs, and database credentials with zero GPU cost.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Tier 1 (Selective NER via <code class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-xs">--features ner</code> or <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">NerDetector</code>):</strong> Attach your own local quantized ONNX/Candle model via <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">VeilEngine::with_ner_detector(...)</code>, or enable the built-in zero-download <code class="text-cyber-cyan font-mono text-xs">HeuristicNerDetector</code> for English/Spanish person names and physical street addresses.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This hybrid architecture delivers sub-millisecond speeds for 95% of requests while reducing downstream NER compute by over 80%.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 7 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-neon/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-neon transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-sm">07.</span>
          How are supply-chain integrity and binary security audited?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-neon transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">pii-veil</code> features continuous Zero-Trust DevSecOps supply-chain certification backed by the <strong class="text-white">GLASTOR® Core</strong> ecosystem:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong class="text-purple-400">GLASTOR® Specter:</strong> Verifies the public API AST in &lt; 5 ms on every pull request, preventing <em>Trojan Breaking Changes</em> and ensuring public method signatures never break unexpectedly in patch releases.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-cyan-400">GLASTOR® Byte-Gauge:</strong> Audits compiled binaries (<code class="text-xs font-mono">veil</code> CLI and WebAssembly) with SIMD-accelerated binary inspection, certifying memory exploit mitigations (<code class="text-xs font-mono">checksec</code>: ASLR/PIE, Stack Canaries, NX/DEP), analyzing Shannon entropy to guarantee zero embedded secrets, and producing <strong class="text-white">SARIF 2.1.0</strong> security scans and <strong class="text-white">CycloneDX 1.5 SBOMs</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Item 8 -->
    <details class="group bg-cyber-card border border-cyber-border rounded-xl p-5 open:border-cyber-neon/60 transition shadow-lg">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none font-bold text-white text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-cyber-neon transition">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-sm">08.</span>
          How do I obtain commercial enterprise support, audits, and guaranteed SLAs?
        </span>
        <span class="text-cyber-muted group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-cyber-neon transition-transform duration-200">
          <span translate="no" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate text-xl">expand_more</span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-cyber-border/60 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans space-y-2">
        <p>
          The core of <code class="text-cyber-neon font-mono text-xs">pii-veil</code> is open-source under dual Apache-2.0 / MIT licenses. For enterprise organizations with critical security requirements, <strong class="text-white">GLASTOR® Core</strong> provides commercial support contracts with 24h down to 4h response SLAs, LLM architecture integration reviews, custom detector engineering, and legal indemnification. Contact us directly at <a href="mailto:founder@glastor.es" class="text-cyber-neon font-mono hover:underline">founder@glastor.es</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
